  2^i+1   : w_k^(1/k) = 0.99932267  -> R = 1 ;  Gamma_k = 1026.0  (= k+2 = 1026, DIVERGES)
  family C: w_k^(1/k) = 0.98654014  -> R = 1 ;  Gamma_k = 5.2301996  (CONVERGES)

  both have R = 1 : True
  Gamma splits    : True
  => 'R >= 1 is exactly the statement that Gamma is finite' is REFUTED

  The true statement:  R > 1  =>  Gamma finite;   Gamma finite  =>  R >= 1;
                       R = 1  =>  undecided, and BOTH cases occur.
  Note the surviving direction is the one prop:nopinch actually uses (R > 1),
  so the proposition's own consequence (item 3, fair coin interior iff R>1) is untouched.
